  {
    "id": "note-9",
    "category": "Body",
    "title": "Chest Masculinization (FTM)",
    "date": "23/01/26",
    "day": "Day 1",
    "speaker": "FTM",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Chest Masculinization Guidelines:**\n\n- **Nipple to IMF Distance > 10 cm**: Indicate Double Incision (DI).\n- **7-10 cm**: With good skin elasticity, DI can be avoided.\n- **< 7 cm**: Counsel for 2-stage procedure (Keyhole first, then Donut).\n\n**Donut Mastopexy Notes:**\n- De-epithelialized skin can retain hair follicles leading to sinus formation.\n- Patient should be on hormones for at least 1 year.\n\n**Double Incision (DI) Tips:**\n- Leave 4cm in the midline.\n- Angle the incision upwards medially to mimic the pectoralis major.\n- Only areola graft ('Dr. Arjun') has better take than total NAC graft.\n- Create a dermal mound in the center.\n- Donut shape is symmetrical; do not aim for a lateral NAC position."
      }
    ],
