  {
    "id": "note-11",
    "category": "Breast",
    "title": "Male to Female Breast Augmentation (Dr. Anand Joshi)",
    "date": "23/01/26",
    "day": "Day 1",
    "speaker": "Dr. Anand Joshi",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Male to Female (MTF) Augmentation**\n\n- Cleavage vs Centralization of implant is key.\n- After 1 year of hormone therapy, skin becomes soft enough for up to 400cc.\n- **Subglandular plane is best.**\n- Gradual increase in size (multiple stages) to reach larger sizes (e.g., 495cc).\n- If seroma doesn't settle -> Explantation.\n- If 1st stage led to symmastia -> Switch to Subpectoral.\n- **Capsular Contracture**: Very low in TG patients (1% vs 10% in cis-females). Possibly due to less commensal bacteria on NAC?"
      }
    ],
    "gallery": [],
