  {
    "id": "note-17",
    "category": "Breast",
    "title": "Mastopexy & Implants (Devinder Singh, Miami)",
    "date": "24/01/26",
    "day": "Day 2",
    "speaker": "Devinder Singh, Miami",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**General Tips:**\n- Preserve fat over pectoral fascia for good lymphatics (Wuringer fascia).\n- **Devinder Singh** advocates for **Subglandular only**.\n- Why subpectoral? Only to hide contracture or old implants.\n- Size: Almost never above 400cc.\n\n**Implant Surface:**\n- Macro texture has higher ALCL risk.\n- 4µm roughness causes least inflammation (e.g., Motiva Smooth Silk).\n\n**Procedure:**\n- Uses balloon and suction device (5 mins)."
      }
    ],
