  {
    "id": "note-19",
    "category": "Breast",
    "title": "Nora Nugent - Secondary Breast Surgery",
    "date": "24/01/26",
    "day": "Day 2",
    "speaker": "",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "media_caption",
        "file": "IMG-20260124-WA0013.jpg",
        "fileType": "image",
        "caption": "**Nora Nugent on Secondary Surgery:**\n- Pre-op video in different positions to ascertain footprint.\n- **Capsule Management**: Can be used as added support for new implant, especially in lax breasts with less tissue.\n- **Reasons to change plane**:\n  - Rippling (poor coverage)\n  - Rupture\n  - Animation deformity\n  - Palpable contracture\n\nIf changing from Subglandular to Dual Plane -> Close the space in the subglandular plane.\n\n**Pocket Reduction:**\n- Stratafix (barbed Monocryl) 4-0 used for lateral pocket reduction.\n- If IMF needs to be raised considerably -> use external net for 4-7 days.\n- Galaflex and Tiger Mesh for better stability."
      },
      {
        "type": "media_caption",
        "file": "IMG-20260124-WA0015.jpg",
        "fileType": "image",
        "caption": "**Photography**: Raised arm picture is essential. Also front bending view."
      }
