  {
    "id": "note-24",
    "category": "Breast",
    "title": "Chiara Botti - Motiva Ergonomix & Transaxillary",
    "date": "24/01/26",
    "day": "Day 2",
    "speaker": "",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Motiva Ergonomix:**\n- 3.2 micrometer smooth surface (Nanotexture).\n- Benefits: No seroma, no double capsule, less irritation/biofilm, no adhesion to capsule (more natural mobility).\n- 0.5% contracture rate.\n- Capsule forms like a thin plastic wrap.\n\n**Placement Technique:**\n- **No Touch**: Irrigate implant with syringe in container -> Shake -> Open -> Insert.\n- Irrigate funnel to activate HA coating.\n- Incision: 3cm for 300cc.\n- Closure with no knots, then tape/dressing."
      },
      {
        "type": "media_caption",
        "file": "IMG-20260124-WA0041.jpg",
        "fileType": "image",
        "caption": "**Transaxillary Approach:**\n- Infiltrate via IMF subglandular first.\n- Scar orientation: Transverse/Oblique. Avoid going too lateral (muscle push).\n- Dissect with retractor handle.\n- Use Dynaplast tape in upper pole + Compression Bra.\n- Note: Since capsule is thin and non-adherent, it falls *with* the breast (no waterfall effect)."
      },
      {
        "type": "media_caption",
        "file": "IMG-20260124-WA0044.jpg",
        "fileType": "image",
        "caption": "Base plate measurement (11cm here). 3cm incision."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Aesthetic Ratio**: 45:55 is widely considered ideal, but no hard rule.\n\n**IMF Fixation**: \n- Raise new IMF 0.5cm higher than target (expect fall).\n- Suturing prep: Dermis -> Scarpa -> Deep Fascia.\n- Can grasp rib periosteum (painful but prevents bottoming out)."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Tuberous Breast**: Score the gland before placing implant. Permanent suture (Nylon) for periareolar block if size diff is large."
      },
      {
        "type": "media_caption",
        "file": "gox-11-e5499.pdf",
        "fileType": "file",
        "caption": "Reference PDF."
      }
    ],
